# AI Workflow
- Always read the `docs/brain.md` file completely before generating any code.
- Always read the `db/db.sql` file completely to understand the db structure before generating any code.
- Always search `docs/brain.md` for implementation patterns before writing any new code.
- CRITICAL: Before writing ANY custom implementation (parsing, conversion, validation, etc.), actively search brain.md for existing utilities, patterns, and parameter types. Never reinvent functionality that already exists in the infrastructure.
- CRITICAL: Before writing ANY database code, search brain.md for "CRITICAL", "loop", and "transaction" to review mandatory patterns. Never execute $Db.executeQuery() inside loops. Never include SELECT queries inside transactions. Always use bulk operations and prepare data in memory before transactions.
- CRITICAL: After writing ANY database code, go through the code review checklist in `docs/code_review_checklist.md` to ensure compliance.
- When requested to create API or API group, any database changes needed, always add to both `db/db.sql` and to `db/UpgradeDB.sql` and Use all the standard flows defined in docs/brain.md
- When adding to `db/UpgradeDB.sql`, always add the changes at the end of the file, assuming all precious script is already deployed on the DB, and do not make changes on the existing script.
- When requested to update the `docs/brain.md` file, always update its Document Version and Last Updated fields.
- Never update `docs/brain.md` with project specific information.
- When creating a new API module (platform/api/*.js and platform/funcs/*.js), always add a corresponding test method in `platform/funcs/api_test.js` that tests all APIs in the new module using $executeAPI and session impersonation.
- When updating an existing API module, always update the corresponding test in `platform/funcs/api_test.js` to ensure it tests the updated functionality correctly.

# Project AI Workflow
- Always read the `docs/project_dev.md` file completely before generating any code.
- Always read the `docs/sds.md` file completely before generating any code.
- Always write to the `docs/project_dev.md` file any new flow added to the project.
- Always read `docs/api_db.sql` and `docs/api_list.md` before generating any code. They contain the recommended API structure and recommended database schema. CRITICAL: Actual implementation can deviate from them if needed.
- Always update `docs/dev_flow.md` file with any progress to the project.

# Style Guide
- Always use tab of 4 spaces for code indentation.
- Always place curly braces on a new line (Allman style).

# SQL Syntax and Style
- Use 'JOIN' instead of 'INNER JOIN'
- Use 'LEFT OUTER JOIN' instead of 'LEFT JOIN'
- Indent JOINs on a new line in one tab more than the 'FROM' clause
- Don't use table aliases if not needed
- Don't use 'AS' keyword for table aliases
- Don't use 'AS' keyword for column aliases
